*spoiler warning*

The only animals you can tame without magical means are domestic=20
animals, these include horses (pony, horse, warhorse), dogs (little dog,=20
dog, large dog) and cats (kitten, housecat, large cat).
The way to tame them is by throwing food to them, but only food they=20
like to eat of course. Horses are herbivores, cats and dogs are=20
carnivores. For the carnivores, any 'meaty', fresh, non-tainted corpse=20
will do, so it's normally very easy to find something (and you already=20
keep a bunch od lizard corpses on you perhaps?). They also gladly eat=20
most 'people food', rations, candy bars, pancakes, etc - not fruit and=20
tins of course. For the herbivores it's much less to choose from,=20
basically 'vegan corpses' (lichen), and fruit.
If you happen upon a non-peaceful domestic animal that poses a threat to=20
you, and you don't have the proper food to tame it, you can throw other=20
food at it, and it will at least become peaceful. Saves you from the=20
imminent danger, and you can return later with proper food if you want=20
to tame it. The food is not consumed in the process.

Then there are many magical means to tame creatures, and ways to turn=20
your already tame creatures into other, hopefully more useful,=20
creatures. But perhaps this was enough spoiling for one day?

